# Transaction

Name the task in the link, say what the person needs first, and say where they are going. Use a transaction page when a task needs context before the native Home Assistant flow or an external service. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it when a household task needs explaining before the native flow opens. Say what the person can do, what they need and where they will go. Common immediate device controls do not need a separate start page.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a task-oriented title and one clear primary destination. A link that opens a flow is navigation. An action that immediately operates a device needs a button and the existing command safeguards ([WG-034](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-034)). Explain any external account or service before the person leaves, and say when a link leaves Home Assistant ([WG-037](../../content/writing-guidelines/add-links.html#wg-037)).

## Home Assistant boundary

This reference does not create device commands or bypass authentication. Prefer "Open theme settings" to a vague "Start now" ([WG-030](../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-titles.html#wg-030)). Do not link to an unverified local route, and do not make a documentation button look as if it operates the household.

